      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "GOD'S HAMMER (6) jumped the race favourite on resumption here and was just fair, sitting midfield and remaining there when beaten 4.5L. Out slightly in trip looks a good move though and he should be better for the fresh effort. Has shown ability at the trials and just needs to bring that to raceday. LAKE BAIKAL (3) got the job done in an impressive performance at Northam, winning by 0.3L after being in the second half of the field. This is tougher, but the 1400m journey now is a big tick on his breeding. Can land the knockout blow again. WINTER BLOOM (9) improved a touch last start, setting the tempo up front and ending up 2.5L off the winner. She's been big odds in both runs, though she's racing well and should give herself every chance with Fiore replacing the apprentice. THE PERSIAN GOD (4) gets the blinkers on first time today and can sit much closer than what we've seen. WESTERN SPLENDOUR (1) won't be far away.",
